# expect: 12
# A NAMED (var-ref) predicate over a wide i64 stream is not monomorphized
# (only inline procs are), so it keeps its dyn param and the filter pull must
# box the wide element back to tagged for the call. Regression guard for the
# predicate-param-rep signal: filter must distinguish inline-typed-wide
# predicates from named/dyn ones (TYPED_CLOSURES_DESIGN.md Phase A).
proc main [] [
  def gt2 [proc [x] [ > $x 2 ]]
  mut i64 s 0
  for [filter [range 1 6] $gt2] z [ set s [+ $s $z] ]   # 3 + 4 + 5 = 12
  print $s
]
main
